1
00:00:22,900 --> 00:00:25,150
You were brilliant, my knight.

2
00:00:25,190 --> 00:00:27,610
[sniffles] Share in my glory,

3
00:00:28,030 --> 00:00:29,820
for it was hard won.

4
00:00:31,240 --> 00:00:32,620
[Xylo grunts softly]

5
00:00:35,870 --> 00:00:37,710
I'd like to speak with you.

6
00:00:37,750 --> 00:00:40,540
Something happened after
you defeated the Demon Lord,

7
00:00:40,580 --> 00:00:42,420
and it directly concerns you.

8
00:00:42,460 --> 00:00:45,420
I am not in the mood
for all that politicking crap.

9
00:00:45,460 --> 00:00:47,630
Makes sense, but regardless,

10
00:00:47,670 --> 00:00:49,840
I need you to hear me out.

11
00:00:50,340 --> 00:00:52,550
♪

12
00:00:52,590 --> 00:00:55,260
[seagulls squawking]

13
00:01:04,860 --> 00:01:07,150
[indistinct chatter]

14
00:01:12,700 --> 00:01:14,660
[MAN 1] Fresh off the hook!

15
00:01:17,790 --> 00:01:20,000
[MAN 2] No. No more,
no more. Please.

16
00:01:20,040 --> 00:01:22,080
[MAN 3]
Let's get moving already!

17
00:01:24,920 --> 00:01:26,460
[door shuts]

18
00:01:42,980 --> 00:01:45,810
[KIVIA] Long story short,
for the time being,

19
00:01:45,860 --> 00:01:48,780
you and Goddess Teoritta
are officially on loan

20
00:01:48,820 --> 00:01:51,150
to the Thirteenth Order
of Holy Knights.

21
00:01:51,650 --> 00:01:54,820
We're "on loan"?
Like a piece of equipment?

22
00:01:55,160 --> 00:01:58,490
The military and the Temple
are still locked in debate,

23
00:01:58,540 --> 00:02:01,370
regarding the goddess'
extraordinary standing.

24
00:02:01,410 --> 00:02:03,830
But your incredible feat
at the fortress,

25
00:02:03,870 --> 00:02:06,710
it's causing a noticeable
sea change.

26
00:02:07,420 --> 00:02:09,960
Xylo, consider this an order.

27
00:02:10,010 --> 00:02:12,010
I want you
to keep protecting her.

28
00:02:12,470 --> 00:02:14,510
If that's really
what you want...

29
00:02:14,550 --> 00:02:15,890
[TEORITTA] Hm?

30
00:02:16,800 --> 00:02:19,430
It's been ages
since we had a day off.

31
00:02:19,470 --> 00:02:21,890
Take us off the front lines
for a change.

32
00:02:21,930 --> 00:02:23,690
[KIVIA] That was
already the plan.

33
00:02:23,730 --> 00:02:24,730
[XYLO] Huh?

34
00:02:24,810 --> 00:02:27,110
I am deploying
your whole hero unit.

35
00:02:27,150 --> 00:02:29,320
You are to protect
Goddess Teoritta.

36
00:02:29,360 --> 00:02:31,070
For now, you will be
stationed here

37
00:02:31,110 --> 00:02:32,190
in Port City Ioff.

38
00:02:32,240 --> 00:02:33,740
[scoffs] In other words,

39
00:02:33,780 --> 00:02:36,200
this place is more dangerous
than a battlefield.

40
00:02:36,240 --> 00:02:38,700
Your assumption's
absolutely right.

41
00:02:38,740 --> 00:02:40,410
There is a faction of heretics

42
00:02:40,450 --> 00:02:42,200
who were expelled
from the Temple,

43
00:02:42,250 --> 00:02:44,750
and they refuse to accept
a new goddess.

44
00:02:45,040 --> 00:02:48,290
They've joined forces with
a religious order of assassins.

45
00:02:48,340 --> 00:02:51,340
-They are plotting to kill--
-[XYLO] Enough, tell me later.

46
00:02:51,380 --> 00:02:52,510
[TEORITTA] My knight!

47
00:02:53,510 --> 00:02:56,050
It is your sacred duty
to protect me!

48
00:02:56,090 --> 00:02:58,390
Alongside our band of heroes,

49
00:02:58,430 --> 00:03:01,060
we shall savor a moment
of respite!

50
00:03:01,100 --> 00:03:02,430
[chuckles]

51
00:03:04,350 --> 00:03:06,150
[paper rustling]

52
00:03:08,520 --> 00:03:10,150
[paper rustling]

53
00:03:10,610 --> 00:03:12,650
[Teoritta snores]

54
00:03:13,610 --> 00:03:15,110
[paper rustling]

55
00:03:19,660 --> 00:03:21,160
-[door slams open]
-[Teoritta gasps]

56
00:03:22,240 --> 00:03:23,500
[XYLO] Hm.

57
00:03:23,790 --> 00:03:25,160
♪

58
00:03:26,370 --> 00:03:27,670
[grunts softly]

59
00:03:28,580 --> 00:03:30,000
[Teoritta grunts softly]

60
00:03:32,590 --> 00:03:34,550
Xylo, rumor has it

61
00:03:34,590 --> 00:03:36,840
you dealt some nasty blows
to the Blight.

62
00:03:36,880 --> 00:03:38,760
Good to see you too, Jayce.

63
00:03:39,140 --> 00:03:41,560
Also I heard about those
three Demon Lords

64
00:03:41,600 --> 00:03:44,390
you erased from existence,
though it sounded like

65
00:03:44,430 --> 00:03:46,890
Dotta and Norgalle
did all the heavy lifting.

66
00:03:46,940 --> 00:03:49,310
I guess Iblis might be
an exception.

67
00:03:49,350 --> 00:03:52,020
Suppose I can accept
that was you.

68
00:03:52,070 --> 00:03:54,190
Meanwhile, I killed two of 'em!

69
00:03:54,230 --> 00:03:56,950
[chuckles] Are you sure
about that number?

70
00:03:56,990 --> 00:03:59,450
Wasn't Rhyno
on the western front with you?

71
00:03:59,490 --> 00:04:01,780
He got nailed
for insubordination.

72
00:04:01,830 --> 00:04:03,490
He'll be locked up a long while.

73
00:04:03,700 --> 00:04:06,750
They're housing a penal hero
in a prison cell?

74
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:09,330
Just admit it. I took out two

75
00:04:09,370 --> 00:04:11,290
while you only managed
to kill one.

76
00:04:11,330 --> 00:04:13,500
I'm the winner
and you're the loser!

77
00:04:13,550 --> 00:04:14,960
Still your wicked tongue!

78
00:04:15,010 --> 00:04:16,760
You are addressing
my knight, knave!

79
00:04:16,800 --> 00:04:18,930
I shall not allow you
to malign him so!

80
00:04:18,970 --> 00:04:20,390
Guessing you're the goddess?

81
00:04:20,430 --> 00:04:22,850
I hear that thief Dotta
found you.

82
00:04:22,890 --> 00:04:26,640
Must be comforting having
a puny kid for a bodyguard.

83
00:04:26,680 --> 00:04:29,440
[Teoritta grunts] The sheer
insolence on display!

84
00:04:29,480 --> 00:04:32,650
Never have I been subject
to such flagrant disrespect!

85
00:04:32,690 --> 00:04:35,480
Easy. Getting angry
won't stop him.

86
00:04:35,530 --> 00:04:37,280
And Dotta didn't find her,

87
00:04:37,320 --> 00:04:40,570
he stole the casket she was in
from the Holy Knights.

88
00:04:40,610 --> 00:04:43,370
[scoffs] I don't see
a big difference.

89
00:04:43,410 --> 00:04:45,870
Like I give a damn
about law and order.

90
00:04:45,910 --> 00:04:48,210
You lost. Time to pony up.

91
00:04:48,250 --> 00:04:50,420
Neely will sulk
if I make her wait.

92
00:04:50,460 --> 00:04:51,670
[Xylo grunts]

93
00:04:52,750 --> 00:04:54,750
[XYLO] Give my regards to Neely.

94
00:04:55,880 --> 00:04:57,670
[Jayce chuckles]

95
00:04:58,420 --> 00:04:59,630
[door slams shut]

96
00:04:59,720 --> 00:05:02,590
My goodness, what is the matter
with that man?

97
00:05:02,640 --> 00:05:04,010
Settle yourself.

98
00:05:04,050 --> 00:05:06,270
That's our unit's dragoon,
Jayce.

99
00:05:06,310 --> 00:05:09,230
He's a fool who grew
and sold illegal substances.

100
00:05:09,270 --> 00:05:11,350
Drugs strong enough
to help dragons.

101
00:05:11,390 --> 00:05:13,350
He was made a hero for that?

102
00:05:13,480 --> 00:05:15,360
[XYLO] That and insurrection.

103
00:05:15,400 --> 00:05:17,440
They say he revolted
against the military

104
00:05:17,480 --> 00:05:19,400
in attempt
to free their dragons.

105
00:05:19,440 --> 00:05:22,490
Uprisings like that
don't usually last a full day,

106
00:05:22,530 --> 00:05:24,870
but Jayce is from
a powerful noble family

107
00:05:24,910 --> 00:05:26,200
and dragons love him.

108
00:05:26,450 --> 00:05:28,450
It escalated beyond reason

109
00:05:28,500 --> 00:05:30,960
and was dubbed
"Jayce's Revolt."

110
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:33,210
So I was correct
in my prior assessment

111
00:05:33,250 --> 00:05:35,630
that hero types
are most eccentric.

112
00:05:41,510 --> 00:05:43,720
Hello.

113
00:05:43,840 --> 00:05:45,140
♪

114
00:05:45,680 --> 00:05:47,390
-[thumps]
-[Xylo grunts]

115
00:05:47,430 --> 00:05:49,720
[grunts] Please,
let us work through this

116
00:05:49,770 --> 00:05:51,730
like rational adults!
With words!

117
00:05:51,770 --> 00:05:52,850
[screams]

118
00:05:53,390 --> 00:05:55,020
It was for your benefit!

119
00:05:55,060 --> 00:05:56,270
Even you have to admit

120
00:05:56,320 --> 00:05:57,980
things would have ended up
a whole lot worse

121
00:05:58,030 --> 00:06:00,820
if the Mastibolt cavalry
hadn't shown up when they did!

122
00:06:00,860 --> 00:06:03,570
I know, and that's why
I'm only gonna hit you twice.

123
00:06:03,610 --> 00:06:06,240
No, Xylo! This is not the time
for violence!

124
00:06:06,280 --> 00:06:07,410
Of course it is.

125
00:06:07,490 --> 00:06:09,660
The little rat is keeping
something from us.

126
00:06:09,700 --> 00:06:11,500
Me? I wouldn't dream of it!

127
00:06:11,540 --> 00:06:13,370
Oh, there is one little thing.

128
00:06:13,410 --> 00:06:15,210
Frenci did ask
to speak with you.

129
00:06:15,250 --> 00:06:16,250
Said she'd murder me

130
00:06:16,380 --> 00:06:18,210
if I didn't make it happen
right away.

131
00:06:18,250 --> 00:06:20,090
I fear my hands are tied.

132
00:06:20,130 --> 00:06:22,840
This Frenci, who might she be?

133
00:06:23,090 --> 00:06:25,340
A noble and my former fiancée.

134
00:06:26,890 --> 00:06:28,060
[TEORITTA] Huh?

135
00:06:29,220 --> 00:06:30,350
♪

136
00:06:32,140 --> 00:06:34,520
Xylo, you are such a mess.

137
00:06:35,190 --> 00:06:36,400
[Teoritta grunts softly]

138
00:06:36,440 --> 00:06:38,150
Why are you acting strangely?

139
00:06:38,190 --> 00:06:39,440
Sit down this instant.

140
00:06:42,070 --> 00:06:44,240
How disappointing
that you haven't improved

141
00:06:44,280 --> 00:06:45,360
in the slightest.

142
00:06:45,400 --> 00:06:47,410
You were on the level
of a fly before,

143
00:06:47,450 --> 00:06:48,870
now a caterpillar.

144
00:06:48,910 --> 00:06:50,040
It's quite grave.

145
00:06:50,080 --> 00:06:51,160
[Xylo sighs]

146
00:06:51,250 --> 00:06:52,910
It wouldn't kill you
to be less insulting

147
00:06:52,950 --> 00:06:54,000
with your comparisons.

148
00:06:54,040 --> 00:06:55,250
Oh, dear.

149
00:06:55,290 --> 00:06:58,250
Do flat-landers consider
pure fact an insult?

150
00:06:58,290 --> 00:07:01,050
I was merely encouraging you
to behave in a manner

151
00:07:01,090 --> 00:07:03,880
that befits a future member
of the Mastibolt family.

152
00:07:03,920 --> 00:07:05,880
Chalk it up
to a cultural difference.

153
00:07:05,930 --> 00:07:07,640
I'll try to remember that.

154
00:07:07,680 --> 00:07:10,640
It was truly not my intention
to cause offense.

155
00:07:13,430 --> 00:07:15,810
Tell me, is she
the goddess in question?

156
00:07:15,850 --> 00:07:17,730
[XYLO] Don't glare.
You'll scare her.

157
00:07:17,770 --> 00:07:19,980
[TEORITTA] I am not afraid
of her whatsoever!

158
00:07:20,020 --> 00:07:21,610
Goddesses have no need of fear!

159
00:07:22,070 --> 00:07:25,530
Indeed. And I'm not glaring,
simply looking.

160
00:07:25,570 --> 00:07:27,990
You are called "Frenci,"
are you not?

161
00:07:28,030 --> 00:07:29,280
Speak truthfully.

162
00:07:29,320 --> 00:07:31,160
What are you to my noble knight?

163
00:07:31,200 --> 00:07:32,830
My former fiancée,

164
00:07:32,870 --> 00:07:34,120
-like I told you.
-[Teoritta grunts]

165
00:07:34,160 --> 00:07:36,370
"Former" is inaccurate.

166
00:07:36,420 --> 00:07:39,500
The oath that binds us
remains intact, Xylo.

167
00:07:39,540 --> 00:07:42,750
Have you just conveniently
forgotten that I'm a hero now?

168
00:07:42,800 --> 00:07:45,130
-We're not allowed to be wed.
-[TEORITTA] Mm-hmm.

169
00:07:45,170 --> 00:07:48,010
Legally, I'm not even considered
an actual human anymore.

170
00:07:48,050 --> 00:07:49,760
Heed my words, Frenci.

171
00:07:49,800 --> 00:07:52,430
This man is a hero as well as
my chosen knight,

172
00:07:52,470 --> 00:07:54,020
and he has irrevocably sworn

173
00:07:54,060 --> 00:07:55,560
to spend
the remainder of his days

174
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:57,690
in reverent adulation of me!

175
00:07:57,730 --> 00:08:00,940
As such, I must
regretfully shatter your dream.

176
00:08:00,980 --> 00:08:02,940
He cannot marry you!

177
00:08:02,980 --> 00:08:06,690
Not again. A curious creature
has taken a liking to you.

178
00:08:06,740 --> 00:08:07,820
This reminds me

179
00:08:07,950 --> 00:08:09,910
of back when my father's
long-eared armadillo

180
00:08:09,950 --> 00:08:11,070
was smitten with you.

181
00:08:11,120 --> 00:08:14,160
Meanwhile, all you got
were scratches.

182
00:08:14,200 --> 00:08:15,750
[FRENCI] That was only because
a western merchant--

183
00:08:15,790 --> 00:08:17,330
Halt! Injustice!

184
00:08:17,370 --> 00:08:19,580
Recounting your shared history
in my presence?

185
00:08:19,620 --> 00:08:21,880
And surely you realize
it is the height of disrespect

186
00:08:21,920 --> 00:08:24,380
to compare a goddess
to a lowly armadillo!

187
00:08:24,420 --> 00:08:25,500
[FRENCI] As I was saying,

188
00:08:25,550 --> 00:08:27,550
our oath remains, and as such,

189
00:08:27,590 --> 00:08:30,050
I am currently attempting
to arrange a pardon for you.

190
00:08:30,090 --> 00:08:31,590
You are? But that's not--

191
00:08:31,640 --> 00:08:34,180
[FRENCI] I will remain
in this city for a while yet,

192
00:08:34,560 --> 00:08:35,770
for good reason.

193
00:08:35,810 --> 00:08:37,270
I refuse to return home

194
00:08:37,310 --> 00:08:39,520
until I've located
the Demon Blight.

195
00:08:39,560 --> 00:08:40,810
[Teoritta gasps]

196
00:08:43,060 --> 00:08:44,690
[XYLO] What do you mean?

197
00:08:44,730 --> 00:08:46,490
[FRENCI] Precisely what I said.

198
00:08:46,530 --> 00:08:48,070
About a month ago,

199
00:08:48,110 --> 00:08:51,110
the night-gaunt chiefs and I
embarked on special maneuvers

200
00:08:51,160 --> 00:08:52,820
to track down a Demon Blight.

201
00:08:52,870 --> 00:08:54,030
A few days ago,

202
00:08:54,280 --> 00:08:57,040
their entire force vanished
somewhere near this town.

203
00:08:57,080 --> 00:08:58,160
[XYLO] Vanished?

204
00:08:58,330 --> 00:09:01,380
That's right.
It was Demon Blight Number 59,

205
00:09:01,420 --> 00:09:04,210
Spriggan, and I have a theory.

206
00:09:04,750 --> 00:09:06,880
It masquerades as human.

207
00:09:07,550 --> 00:09:09,880
Demon Lords can appear human?

208
00:09:09,920 --> 00:09:11,050
Is that so?

209
00:09:11,090 --> 00:09:13,930
It's a rare trait even among
Demon Lords.

210
00:09:13,970 --> 00:09:15,970
Annoying. What a damn headache.

211
00:09:16,520 --> 00:09:19,770
[FRENCI] It's possible it has
infiltrated the city by now.

212
00:09:20,140 --> 00:09:21,350
Tread carefully.

213
00:09:21,400 --> 00:09:23,270
The creature
has already laid waste

214
00:09:23,310 --> 00:09:24,980
to one of our territories.

215
00:09:25,360 --> 00:09:28,440
Anyhow, this concludes
our discussion.

216
00:09:30,570 --> 00:09:33,660
May I ask who has been
eavesdropping in the corner?

217
00:09:33,700 --> 00:09:36,370
Sorry, I have to supervise.

218
00:09:36,990 --> 00:09:38,330
It's a rule.

219
00:09:38,370 --> 00:09:40,870
I must ensure there isn't
any suspicious activity.

220
00:09:40,910 --> 00:09:43,380
I see. Farewell then.

221
00:09:43,420 --> 00:09:46,920
I suggest you come up
with a better excuse next time.

222
00:09:54,890 --> 00:09:57,220
[TEORITTA]
I deeply desire to indulge!

223
00:09:57,260 --> 00:09:59,640
Venetim and Dotta
told me about it.

224
00:09:59,680 --> 00:10:01,270
The west and north sides
of the city

225
00:10:01,310 --> 00:10:03,520
are filled with stalls
selling rare goods,

226
00:10:03,560 --> 00:10:05,360
and every bite of food
is completely free!

227
00:10:05,400 --> 00:10:08,940
It's only free for someone
with sticky fingers like Dotta.

228
00:10:08,980 --> 00:10:11,360
We're not going sightseeing,
and that's final.

229
00:10:11,740 --> 00:10:13,450
We're here for a purpose,

230
00:10:13,490 --> 00:10:15,320
to lure out
those Temple heretics

231
00:10:15,370 --> 00:10:17,280
who are after you,
and arrest them.

232
00:10:17,330 --> 00:10:19,790
Verily, I am well-aware
of your noble plan

233
00:10:19,830 --> 00:10:21,040
to protect your goddess!

234
00:10:21,080 --> 00:10:22,790
[sighs] Listen carefully.

235
00:10:23,460 --> 00:10:25,790
The Holy Sword is our secret.

236
00:10:27,920 --> 00:10:30,380
If those Galtuile bastards
find out,

237
00:10:30,420 --> 00:10:31,800
our lives will get a lot harder.

238
00:10:31,840 --> 00:10:33,510
There is no need to fret!

239
00:10:33,550 --> 00:10:36,260
For I am a goddess, after all.
I know just what to do!

240
00:10:36,300 --> 00:10:37,550
[Xylo sighs]

241
00:10:37,600 --> 00:10:39,930
I'll join you two
on your excursion.

242
00:10:39,970 --> 00:10:42,390
I'm prepared to be
the goddess' sword and shield,

243
00:10:42,430 --> 00:10:43,770
if need be.

244
00:10:43,940 --> 00:10:45,020
[Teoritta groans]

245
00:10:45,230 --> 00:10:46,440
[XYLO] It's settled.

246
00:10:46,980 --> 00:10:49,400
I wonder who else
we should bring along.

247
00:10:49,440 --> 00:10:50,440
[Venetim humming]

248
00:10:50,690 --> 00:10:51,990
[XYLO] Venetim's worthless
as a bodyguard.

249
00:10:52,030 --> 00:10:54,320
I can't let Dotta loose in town

250
00:10:54,360 --> 00:10:56,860
unless I tie his hands
behind his back.

251
00:10:56,950 --> 00:10:59,200
His Majesty
would probably insist

252
00:10:59,240 --> 00:11:00,870
we act as his royal guard.

253
00:11:00,910 --> 00:11:03,500
-As for Tatsuya...
-[birds chirping]

254
00:11:03,700 --> 00:11:05,460
[XYLO]... that's a bad idea.

255
00:11:06,210 --> 00:11:08,960
Hate to say it,
we're low on options.

256
00:11:09,290 --> 00:11:10,300
♪

257
00:11:10,340 --> 00:11:12,550
[hammering]

258
00:11:13,510 --> 00:11:15,720
-[hammering continues]
-[Jayce grunting]

259
00:11:19,050 --> 00:11:20,930
These morons
honestly expect me

260
00:11:20,970 --> 00:11:22,970
to keep Neely in this dump?
Bastards.

261
00:11:23,020 --> 00:11:24,850
The least they can do
is give her enough room

262
00:11:24,890 --> 00:11:26,440
to spread her wings and tail.

263
00:11:26,480 --> 00:11:28,440
I agree, it is critical.

264
00:11:28,480 --> 00:11:30,650
By the way, I have
important commander work

265
00:11:30,690 --> 00:11:33,360
that needs tending to,
so I'll just take my leave.

266
00:11:33,730 --> 00:11:36,820
Who's the most powerful force
in this entire unit?

267
00:11:37,070 --> 00:11:39,620
Without question,
it's you and Neely.

268
00:11:43,200 --> 00:11:47,080
In that case, do your part
to keep her in prime condition,

269
00:11:47,120 --> 00:11:49,080
and shut your mouth, conman.

270
00:11:49,750 --> 00:11:51,590
Hold on a little longer, Neely.

271
00:11:51,630 --> 00:11:54,090
I'll have a nice bed ready
for you soon.

272
00:11:54,130 --> 00:11:55,590
[Neely huffs]

273
00:11:56,420 --> 00:11:59,390
Hm? [chuckles] Don't worry
about the other dragons,

274
00:11:59,430 --> 00:12:01,930
I was simply measuring them
out of curiosity,

275
00:12:01,970 --> 00:12:04,350
and I didn't take a peek
under any of their wings.

276
00:12:04,390 --> 00:12:06,350
You know,
I wouldn't dare do that.

277
00:12:06,390 --> 00:12:07,440
Believe me.

278
00:12:07,480 --> 00:12:08,690
[Neely growls softly]

279
00:12:09,270 --> 00:12:10,230
[JAYCE]
I've never lied to you...

280
00:12:10,270 --> 00:12:12,320
This could go on for forever.

281
00:12:12,360 --> 00:12:13,570
[VENETIM] I need some help here!

282
00:12:13,610 --> 00:12:14,900
-[crashing]
-[Venetim yelps]

283
00:12:14,940 --> 00:12:17,700
Looks like we're down
to our last option.

284
00:12:17,740 --> 00:12:20,240
-[bell tolling]
-[indistinct chatter]

285
00:12:31,880 --> 00:12:33,550
[TSAV] Take my word for it, bro,

286
00:12:33,590 --> 00:12:35,550
those guys
are the absolute worst!

287
00:12:35,590 --> 00:12:38,170
Gwen Mohsa calls itself
a "religious order."

288
00:12:38,220 --> 00:12:41,050
I know they raised me and all,
but a fact is still a fact.

289
00:12:41,090 --> 00:12:43,680
Even I could always tell
they were pure evil.

290
00:12:43,720 --> 00:12:45,560
I'm talkin' human sacrifice,

291
00:12:45,600 --> 00:12:47,390
offering up kids
to the goddesses.

292
00:12:47,430 --> 00:12:49,690
And don't get me started
on "Holy Communion,"

293
00:12:49,730 --> 00:12:51,270
-which meant--
-Enough already.

294
00:12:51,310 --> 00:12:52,400
[TSAV] Fine.

295
00:12:52,440 --> 00:12:54,020
If he's going
to prattle on like that,

296
00:12:54,070 --> 00:12:56,690
why did we even
bother with disguises?

297
00:12:57,150 --> 00:12:58,490
On that subject...

298
00:12:59,240 --> 00:13:01,160
[MAN] Hey, wait, wait!
Come back!

299
00:13:01,200 --> 00:13:03,410
-[XYLO] Well done.
-[KIVIA] Uh?

300
00:13:03,780 --> 00:13:06,410
Brilliant choice
to dress as a man.

301
00:13:06,450 --> 00:13:08,160
It's the perfect disguise.

302
00:13:09,830 --> 00:13:11,000
[Kivia grunts softly]

303
00:13:12,130 --> 00:13:13,960
[TEORITTA] Come hither, Xylo!

304
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:16,340
I wish for us to purchase
a keepsake,

305
00:13:16,380 --> 00:13:17,920
in commemoration.

306
00:13:17,960 --> 00:13:19,470
[XYLO] Of what, exactly?

307
00:13:19,510 --> 00:13:21,470
The very first time
a great goddess

308
00:13:21,510 --> 00:13:23,890
and her equally great knight
blessed these city streets

309
00:13:23,930 --> 00:13:24,930
with their presence.

310
00:13:24,970 --> 00:13:26,850
I should have known.

311
00:13:26,890 --> 00:13:28,890
Well, what do you want?

312
00:13:28,930 --> 00:13:31,560
I insist that we make
our selection together!

313
00:13:31,600 --> 00:13:34,610
After all, it is a prize
for both of us. [chuckles]

314
00:13:35,060 --> 00:13:36,110
♪

315
00:13:36,150 --> 00:13:37,280
[indistinct chatter]

316
00:13:39,530 --> 00:13:41,360
Perhaps this fabric
would suffice.

317
00:13:41,400 --> 00:13:43,950
Behold how it shimmers
when held in the light!

318
00:13:43,990 --> 00:13:46,330
I'm guessing that was
brought here from the west,

319
00:13:46,370 --> 00:13:49,200
across Korio Bay.
They have lots of unique wares.

320
00:13:49,250 --> 00:13:51,580
[TEORITTA] Look, a bracelet!

321
00:13:51,620 --> 00:13:53,920
I dare say that piece
is worthy of a goddess.

322
00:13:53,960 --> 00:13:55,340
It looks like jade.

323
00:13:55,380 --> 00:13:57,460
You could buy a house
for the same price.

324
00:13:57,500 --> 00:13:59,380
We'd better keep Dotta far away.

325
00:13:59,420 --> 00:14:01,470
I did not inquire
about the price.

326
00:14:01,510 --> 00:14:04,430
And this matter
does not concern Dotta. Hmph!

327
00:14:04,470 --> 00:14:08,100
Hey, Tsav, what would you do
if you were the assassin?

328
00:14:08,140 --> 00:14:11,230
Um, I'd probably mix in
with the crowd,

329
00:14:11,270 --> 00:14:13,600
then a little quick slash
as I walked past?

330
00:14:14,100 --> 00:14:15,400
Listen well!

331
00:14:15,560 --> 00:14:17,730
Your goddess hereby decrees
that you should be giving

332
00:14:17,770 --> 00:14:19,900
your full attention
to picking out our keepsake!

333
00:14:19,940 --> 00:14:20,940
[XYLO] Understood.

334
00:14:20,990 --> 00:14:22,070
♪

335
00:14:27,870 --> 00:14:30,450
[XYLO] Finally,
something I can appreciate.

336
00:14:30,500 --> 00:14:31,660
Have you chosen?

337
00:14:31,710 --> 00:14:32,830
Never mind.

338
00:14:32,870 --> 00:14:34,870
It's dangerous
to give children weapons.

339
00:14:34,920 --> 00:14:36,000
Utter nonsense!

340
00:14:36,040 --> 00:14:38,750
You shall instruct me.
Select my blade!

341
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:41,210
Let's go with...

342
00:14:42,340 --> 00:14:44,050
[Xylo grunts softly]

343
00:14:44,090 --> 00:14:45,720
This one here.

344
00:14:47,260 --> 00:14:48,390
[Teoritta exclaims]

345
00:14:49,930 --> 00:14:51,390
How magnificent.

346
00:14:51,430 --> 00:14:52,980
It is beautiful.

347
00:14:54,520 --> 00:14:56,400
We'll purchase the knife.

348
00:14:57,100 --> 00:14:58,860
And that, too.

349
00:14:59,230 --> 00:15:00,820
You take scrip?

350
00:15:01,150 --> 00:15:02,440
[Xylo grunts]

351
00:15:06,610 --> 00:15:09,330
It's yours. And keep it
at the ready.

352
00:15:09,370 --> 00:15:10,280
I shall.

353
00:15:10,330 --> 00:15:12,040
[♪ tense music playing]

354
00:15:16,460 --> 00:15:18,380
-[Teoritta gasps]
-[Kivia grunts]

355
00:15:23,800 --> 00:15:27,220
-[assassin screaming]
-[crowd gasping]

356
00:15:27,260 --> 00:15:29,050
[chokes]

357
00:15:32,390 --> 00:15:34,100
[woman whimpers]

358
00:15:34,140 --> 00:15:36,390
[woman screams]

359
00:15:39,400 --> 00:15:40,940
[Teoritta gasps softly]

360
00:15:40,980 --> 00:15:43,940
Ooh, lookie here. Spoils of war.

361
00:15:47,320 --> 00:15:49,780
Xylo, switch
to the alternate route!

362
00:15:49,820 --> 00:15:52,120
Got it. Let's get moving.

363
00:15:52,700 --> 00:15:54,830
Does that mean
the battle is afoot?

364
00:15:55,330 --> 00:15:58,040
[XYLO] Afraid so.
We'll call this sightseeing.

365
00:16:15,060 --> 00:16:16,680
What the hell's going on here?

366
00:16:16,730 --> 00:16:18,190
Where are all the Holy Knights?

367
00:16:18,230 --> 00:16:19,650
This is not good.

368
00:16:19,690 --> 00:16:21,860
Something must have happened
to them all.

369
00:16:21,900 --> 00:16:24,940
Don't worry. Those guys weren't
religious-order assassins,

370
00:16:24,980 --> 00:16:26,570
and it was so obvious
they didn't have

371
00:16:26,610 --> 00:16:28,450
any real training
under their belts.

372
00:16:28,490 --> 00:16:29,490
Stay sharp.

373
00:16:30,030 --> 00:16:32,450
For all we know, they could be
allies of the Demon Blight.

374
00:16:32,910 --> 00:16:35,080
[Xylo exhales] Coexisters.

375
00:16:35,990 --> 00:16:38,120
[KIVIA] Regardless,
it's someone who benefits

376
00:16:38,160 --> 00:16:39,670
from the goddess' death.

377
00:16:39,710 --> 00:16:42,710
I didn't think they had
infiltrated the military.

378
00:16:43,040 --> 00:16:44,300
[Tsav gasps]

379
00:16:44,500 --> 00:16:45,630
[Tsav grunts]

380
00:16:46,760 --> 00:16:48,550
Freaky! Stay back!

381
00:16:50,840 --> 00:16:51,930
[Tsav gasps]

382
00:16:56,180 --> 00:16:58,770
[Tsav grunts]
Who the hell are you?

383
00:16:59,100 --> 00:17:00,850
[Tsav pants]

384
00:17:02,310 --> 00:17:04,650
[TSAV] She's got some
filthy tricks, bro.

385
00:17:04,690 --> 00:17:06,190
Real nasty.

386
00:17:07,900 --> 00:17:09,450
This pain is brutal!

387
00:17:09,780 --> 00:17:11,870
They have come.
What to do?

388
00:17:12,070 --> 00:17:14,700
Remain here.
We'll end this quickly.

389
00:17:14,740 --> 00:17:15,950
♪

390
00:17:26,710 --> 00:17:27,840
[assassin grunts]

391
00:17:30,130 --> 00:17:31,550
[assassin grunts]

392
00:17:40,020 --> 00:17:41,810
-[Kivia grunts]
-[XYLO] Stay back.

393
00:17:47,030 --> 00:17:48,320
[both grunts]

394
00:17:52,240 --> 00:17:54,240
[grunts] A seal compound?

395
00:17:56,450 --> 00:17:58,450
Surprise.

396
00:18:03,580 --> 00:18:04,670
Can you fight?

397
00:18:04,710 --> 00:18:06,380
Who do you think
you're talking to?

398
00:18:06,420 --> 00:18:08,500
Stay silent and on your guard.

399
00:18:11,220 --> 00:18:12,300
[Xylo grunts]

400
00:18:12,340 --> 00:18:15,260
[MAN] That is quite enough,
Shiji Bau.

401
00:18:15,300 --> 00:18:17,100
You're up against
the penal hero

402
00:18:17,140 --> 00:18:18,770
who is pacted with a goddess.

403
00:18:18,810 --> 00:18:21,310
Your chances of victory
are one in a thousand.

404
00:18:21,730 --> 00:18:23,770
It is time to withdraw.

405
00:18:24,850 --> 00:18:27,570
Are you even
listening to me, Shiji Bau?

406
00:18:27,610 --> 00:18:29,900
You amateur,
think before you speak.

407
00:18:29,940 --> 00:18:32,530
You cannot just go around
saying our names.

408
00:18:32,570 --> 00:18:33,610
Got it, Boojum?

409
00:18:33,650 --> 00:18:36,240
Is that so?
I truly had no idea.

410
00:18:36,280 --> 00:18:38,910
I've yet to learn
the fine details of the trade.

411
00:18:38,950 --> 00:18:41,830
Given your experience, I hope
you'll continue to teach me--

412
00:18:41,870 --> 00:18:42,960
Please hurry up, sir!

413
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:44,460
Before the Holy Knights
show up!

414
00:18:44,670 --> 00:18:45,830
[BOOJUM] Be quiet.

415
00:18:45,920 --> 00:18:48,460
Can you not tell
that I am talking to someone?

416
00:18:48,500 --> 00:18:50,800
It's rather rude to interrupt,
don't you see?

417
00:18:50,840 --> 00:18:53,010
-[grunts]
-[Teoritta gasps]

418
00:18:53,880 --> 00:18:57,430
Remember, we were told to avoid
unnecessary casualties.

419
00:18:57,470 --> 00:18:59,140
[BOOJUM] Casualties?

420
00:18:59,180 --> 00:19:00,720
Ah, but I didn't kill him.

421
00:19:00,770 --> 00:19:02,310
That would be uncouth.

422
00:19:02,930 --> 00:19:04,940
You ripped his jaw clean off.

423
00:19:04,980 --> 00:19:06,600
There is something wrong
with you.

424
00:19:06,650 --> 00:19:08,900
That much is apparent.

425
00:19:09,360 --> 00:19:10,780
Kivia!

426
00:19:11,650 --> 00:19:12,940
[KIVIA] Niskeph!

427
00:19:15,110 --> 00:19:16,490
[Shiji Bau grunts]

428
00:19:18,160 --> 00:19:20,740
[BOOJUM] Refrain from using
lightning staves.

429
00:19:20,790 --> 00:19:22,620
Getting shot in the back...

430
00:19:22,660 --> 00:19:23,830
stings.

431
00:19:26,620 --> 00:19:27,670
[Xylo grunts]

432
00:19:53,650 --> 00:19:55,740
Are you Xylo Forbartz?

433
00:19:55,780 --> 00:19:58,070
As in the infamous penal hero?

434
00:19:58,410 --> 00:19:59,620
Who's asking?

435
00:19:59,660 --> 00:20:01,410
I think she called you "Boojum"?

436
00:20:01,450 --> 00:20:03,330
Did you escape a circus troupe?

437
00:20:03,370 --> 00:20:04,410
[BOOJUM] I did not.

438
00:20:04,750 --> 00:20:06,870
You're quite the exceptional
knife-thrower, though.

439
00:20:06,910 --> 00:20:09,000
Perhaps you should have
joined a circus troupe.

440
00:20:09,040 --> 00:20:11,920
I did, and for three years
to boot.

441
00:20:11,960 --> 00:20:13,960
My specialty was
the flying trapeze.

442
00:20:14,010 --> 00:20:15,260
Is that so?

443
00:20:15,300 --> 00:20:16,670
That explains it.

444
00:20:16,760 --> 00:20:19,720
I can assure you without even
a sliver of exaggeration

445
00:20:19,760 --> 00:20:21,890
that you're the best
I've ever seen.

446
00:20:22,640 --> 00:20:24,520
You have my respect.

447
00:20:24,930 --> 00:20:27,230
Seriously, just stop talking.

448
00:20:27,270 --> 00:20:29,770
Never willingly volunteer
information.

449
00:20:29,810 --> 00:20:31,810
A solid point.
I am pleased to say

450
00:20:31,860 --> 00:20:33,320
I'm learning a lot
from you today.

451
00:20:33,360 --> 00:20:35,860
We're in a real predicament
here, guys.

452
00:20:35,900 --> 00:20:37,070
That tricksy broad?

453
00:20:37,320 --> 00:20:40,030
She just so happens to be
a world-famous adventurer.

454
00:20:40,110 --> 00:20:42,240
I bet she has
an even better kill rate

455
00:20:42,280 --> 00:20:43,740
on her hits than you do.

456
00:20:43,780 --> 00:20:46,500
Probably! But my numbers
would be through the roof,

457
00:20:46,540 --> 00:20:48,330
if I weren't
such a big old softie.

458
00:20:48,370 --> 00:20:49,870
[Teoritta panting]

459
00:20:50,790 --> 00:20:51,830
Is it time?

460
00:20:51,880 --> 00:20:53,460
Shall I call down
a rain of swords?

461
00:20:53,500 --> 00:20:54,670
You'd better not.

462
00:20:54,710 --> 00:20:56,340
Would it not be prudent
to do so?

463
00:20:56,380 --> 00:20:59,590
I know how painful it is
for a goddess to harm a human.

464
00:20:59,630 --> 00:21:01,340
And I refuse to do that to you.

465
00:21:01,800 --> 00:21:04,350
That is true,
yet something is amiss.

466
00:21:04,390 --> 00:21:06,520
I have the strangest feeling
that he...

467
00:21:06,560 --> 00:21:09,230
-[whooshing]
-Look up, bro! Incoming!

468
00:21:09,270 --> 00:21:11,810
Perfect. Right on cue.

469
00:21:12,190 --> 00:21:13,440
[Teoritta gasps]

470
00:21:22,070 --> 00:21:25,080
[assassins screaming]

471
00:21:28,080 --> 00:21:30,500
[assassin screams] Help me.

472
00:21:34,170 --> 00:21:35,590
[Teoritta gasps]

473
00:21:38,970 --> 00:21:40,380
Well?

474
00:21:40,420 --> 00:21:42,970
We came to this dingy place
like you asked.

475
00:21:43,010 --> 00:21:44,850
Now show Neely some gratitude.

476
00:21:44,890 --> 00:21:47,060
Of course. Thank you, Neely.

477
00:21:47,100 --> 00:21:49,310
Thanks, Big Sis Neely!
Good work!

478
00:21:49,350 --> 00:21:50,480
[Neely huffs]

479
00:21:50,520 --> 00:21:53,350
Attagirl! We don't deserve
your kindness.

480
00:21:53,400 --> 00:21:55,860
And I promise we'll have
a day off real soon.

481
00:21:55,900 --> 00:21:58,070
We'll go and fly
over the sea tomorrow.

482
00:21:58,110 --> 00:21:59,820
-[Neely grunts]
-[Jayce exclaims]

483
00:22:00,190 --> 00:22:01,740
[BOOJUM] How curious.

484
00:22:01,780 --> 00:22:05,120
Seems dragon flames
are difficult to endure.

485
00:22:05,160 --> 00:22:06,280
[Xylo gasps]

486
00:22:08,910 --> 00:22:11,580
[BOOJUM] I do not have
enough blood.

487
00:22:11,620 --> 00:22:13,670
This was informative.

488
00:22:13,710 --> 00:22:16,090
I will be taking my leave now.

489
00:22:16,130 --> 00:22:17,630
Farewell.

490
00:22:18,880 --> 00:22:20,010
[Kivia grunts softly]

491
00:22:20,170 --> 00:22:21,630
[Tsav grunts]

492
00:22:22,130 --> 00:22:23,680
What's that guy's deal?

493
00:22:23,720 --> 00:22:26,640
No way he should have survived
Neely's flame.

494
00:22:27,850 --> 00:22:29,020
Teoritta,

495
00:22:29,060 --> 00:22:31,310
right before
you were interrupted,

496
00:22:31,350 --> 00:22:33,560
what were you saying
about that man?

497
00:22:34,310 --> 00:22:36,770
It is most difficult
to put it to words.

498
00:22:36,810 --> 00:22:38,900
I found that,
for some strange reason,

499
00:22:38,940 --> 00:22:40,730
I felt surprisingly unhesitant

500
00:22:40,780 --> 00:22:43,200
when faced with the notion
of attacking him.

501
00:22:45,410 --> 00:22:46,950
It is possible,

502
00:22:46,990 --> 00:22:48,740
the man we just fought,

503
00:22:48,780 --> 00:22:50,740
was Demon Lord Spriggan.

504
00:23:00,840 --> 00:23:03,470
[♪ closing theme song playing]
